{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Use emergency phone alerts to help find missing children in the UK",
        "additional_details": "The UK already has a location-based Emergency Alerts system. I want the Government to establish a clear national protocol allowing police to use it for high-risk, missing-child cases, similar to Amber Alerts. Where police believe a child is in immediate danger, people in the relevant area should receive an alert with approved identifying details, the last known location and clear instructions on how to report information.",
        "background": "Create a UK Amber Alert-style system allowing police to send emergency mobile alerts to people in relevant areas when a missing child is believed to be at serious risk. Alerts should include key identifying details and information that could help the public assist police.",
